@startuml retention-v2-format
' ============================================================================
' The shared retention V2 format (task 7923): the objects a catalog slot
' appoints, frozen in rspace++/src/rspace/persistence/retention/v2_format.rs
' and modeled in formal/rocq/stack_safe_pda/theories/RetentionV2Format.v.
'   GREY    #616161  the catalog slot, whose envelope V2 does not change
'   AMBER   #EF6C00  the V1 retention manifest, which stays readable
'   GREEN   #2E7D32  the V2 metadata objects: the anchor and the radix nodes
'   PURPLE  #6A1B9A  the semantic state manifests both formats name
'   BLUE    #1565C0  the 48-byte retention key
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ObjectBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ObjectFontSize 13
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64

title <b>The shared retention V2 format</b>\nthe catalog's opaque retention reference appoints either a V1 manifest or a V2 anchor

object "Catalog slot · RSpaceCatalogV1 · 336 bytes" as Slot #E0E0E0 {
  0..16 domain · 16..24 version 1
  48..96 current state: generation, manifest reference
  168..176 commit length: 384 or 400
  <b>216..256 retention reference: digest, length</b>
  256..264 reserved · 280..288 flags · 288..328 reserved
  328..336 CRC32C
}

object "V1 retention manifest · RSpaceDAG.Retn" as V1 #FFE0B2 {
  32-byte envelope
  current entry: 56 bytes
  historical count: u64
  historical entries: 56 bytes each, strictly increasing
}

object "V2 retention anchor · RSpaceDAG.RetA · 136 bytes" as Anchor #C8E6C9 {
  32-byte envelope (body 104)
  current entry: 56 bytes, the V1 entry verbatim
  historical count <latex>n</latex>: u64, little-endian
  historical root: ObjectRefV1, 40 bytes
}

object "Empty radix node · RSpaceDAG.RetR · 50 bytes" as Empty #DCEDC8 {
  the canonical empty DAG body
  appointed exactly when <latex>n = 0</latex>
  digest 50e61ba0…
}

object "Radix inner node · RSpaceDAG.RetR" as Inner #DCEDC8 {
  the canonical DAG node body, unchanged
  prefix shorter than the remaining key
  endpoint Absent
  two or more children, strictly increasing edges
}

object "Radix leaf · RSpaceDAG.RetR" as Leaf #DCEDC8 {
  prefix = every remaining key byte
  endpoint Multiplicity(claim), claim <latex>\ge</latex> manifest length
  no children
}

object "Retention key · 48 bytes" as Key #BBDEFB {
  0..8 generation, big-endian
  8..40 manifest digest
  40..48 manifest length, big-endian
}

object "Semantic state manifest · RSpaceDAG.SMan" as SMan #E1BEE7 {
  data-bag, continuation-map and join-bag roots
}

Slot -[#616161]-> SMan : current state
Slot -[#EF6C00]-> V1 : retention reference\n(V1 publication)
Slot -[#2E7D32]-> Anchor : retention reference\n(V2 publication)
Anchor -[#2E7D32]-> Empty : root when <latex>n = 0</latex>
Anchor -[#2E7D32]-> Leaf : root when <latex>n = 1</latex>
Anchor -[#2E7D32]-> Inner : root when <latex>n \ge 2</latex>
Inner -[#2E7D32]-> Inner : edge byte
Inner -[#2E7D32]-> Leaf : edge byte
Leaf .[#1565C0].> Key : path bytes followed by\nthe prefix spell the key
Key .[#6A1B9A].> SMan : decodes to the state\n(generation, manifest reference)
V1 .[#6A1B9A].> SMan : each entry names\na state manifest

note right of Anchor #F1F8E9
  <b>Metadata closure</b> <latex>M</latex>: the anchor and every radix node reachable
  from its root; <latex>|M| \ge 2</latex> and at least 186 bytes.
  <b>V2 checkpoint</b> (domain RSpaceDAG.Chkp2, same 216-byte layout):
  DATA = retained semantic objects <latex>R</latex> plus <latex>M</latex>, a disjoint union.
  The V1 rule, DATA objects = <latex>|R| + 1</latex>, refuses every V2 inventory.
end note

note bottom of Leaf #F1F8E9
  <latex>n</latex> counts entry occurrences, not leaf objects:
  equal claims under equal suffixes share one leaf.
end note
@enduml
